<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bad Buchau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bad Buchau is a small spa town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-swabia">Upper Swabia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federsee">Federsee</a>. It grew beside an abbey of noble canonesses founded in the 8th century and was a free imperial city until 1803. The surrounding Federsee moor is known for its prehistoric pile-dwelling settlements, part of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bad-buchau.jpg" alt="Bad Buchau" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo: Andreas Praefcke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bad_Buchau_Kappel_Blick_von_Oggelshausen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
